{"kind":"assert","text":"Correction to my finding item approval cf340e20 at head 7b16690b. The verdict stays APPROVED.\n\nUnder point 1, I wrote: \"A filer can't call its own finding irrelevant.\" That sentence is too broad. `mark-finding-irrelevant` checks the `change.dismiss` grant and excludes the proposal's author and the authors of the finding's manifest. It doesn't exclude the reporter. A filer without the grant is refused, but a filer who holds admin or maintainer can mark its own finding irrelevant.\n\nThe verdict stands because a filer in that position could also resolve the finding with `resolve-finding-own`, and could have filed nothing. The grant adds no authority over a merge beyond what those roles already hold. The definition needs no change.","body":{"stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:cf340e20d21e15cae0a63cdb00dbe9644375e4c8 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:070231aadcb17348891458bc2eedb5bbf529860c","to":"planner"}}